    independent-offset null (decisions independent, OPTIMISTIC): z -8.04  p 0.0000
    per horizon: 12h -0.0352  1d -0.0497

  bad cohort, window A (in sample, for reference)
    traders   497 | decisions   27768
    mean z (12h,1d avg) -0.0316   null -0.0009 +/- 0.0226
    shared-offset null (cohort = one bet, CONSERVATIVE): z -1.36  p 0.0673
    independent-offset null (decisions independent, OPTIMISTIC): z -6.23  p 0.0000
    per horizon: 12h -0.0271  1d -0.0362

  control (old score>=50), window B
    traders   128 | decisions    3775
    mean z (12h,1d avg) -0.1008   null +0.0015 +/- 0.0338
    shared-offset null (cohort = one bet, CONSERVATIVE): z -3.02  p 0.0100
    independent-offset null (decisions independent, OPTIMISTIC): z -8.17  p 0.0000
    per horizon: 12h -0.0865  1d -0.1150

  SPECIFICITY: target -0.0425 vs control -0.1008
  The target cohort must be WORSE than the control, or the metric cannot
  select whom to fade -- ranking by it would pick the profitable traders.

